body:
Speaking of matrix, I would suggest adding scale modifier into the shader.
Having to manually edit the matrix is rather cumbersome and I assume that it will be frequently prerequisite for other effects like adding outline or glow. On the other hand, adding rotations seems like overkill to me that should probably be done by modifying the uniform projection from the script.

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f44a462-5643-458f-aea1-397e001a2f9a)
![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b035a43-f50a-4d02-9115-481f63f76e67)


```
shader_type mesh_rasterizer;

uniform float scale = 1.0;
uniform mat4 projection;
uniform sampler2D base_texture: source_color;

void vertex() {
	mat4 scale_matrix = mat4(
		vec4(scale,0.0,0.0,0.0),
		vec4(0.0,scale,0.0,0.0),
		vec4(0.0,0.0,scale,0.0),
		vec4(0.0,0.0,0.0,1.0)
	);
    VERTEX = projection * scale_matrix * VERTEX;
}
void fragment() {
    COLOR = texture(base_texture, UV);
}

```

Implemented drawable texture in my opinion that works with the mesh rasterizer. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12443#issuecomment-2899821896

In addition: 
- Custom blend state via `RasterizerBlendState` (almost the same with `RDPipelineColorBlendStateAttachment`).
- All possiable RD texture format that supported by Godot.
- MSAA.

TODO:
Waiting for more feedback and unify this PR with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701. As I focus on RD render and not familiar with compatibility renderer, not sure if these features are suitable for compatibility renderer.

In addition, this PR chooses to do nothing for the conversion between sRGB and linear( source_color hint also does nothing ). There is a difference in RGBAF/RGBAH texture colors in the 2D and 3D renderers. But RGBA8/RGBA8_SRGB textures displays the same in 2D and 3D. I think it's expected.

